  "summary_text": "Kyle, yesterday was a study in two different stories. Port Washington had a soft day\u2014grooming down 8% and overall traffic down 11%\u2014but retail surged 52%, suggesting customers came for something specific and found it. Hicksville, meanwhile, had a breakout day: revenue up 48%, both grooming and retail accelerating sharply, and transactions up 85%. This is worth attention. Week-to-date, Hicksville is running +47% while Port Washington is -6%, which tells us momentum is shifting toward the newer location.\n\nThe bigger picture is strong. Year-to-date you're up 53% in revenue and 56% in appointments across both stores. April is tracking ahead of March, which means spring demand is real and you're capturing it. Port Washington's weakness yesterday looks like noise, not a trend\u2014the month is still solidly positive.\n\nTwo operational issues: both locations are out of the same high-velocity items (bully sticks at Port Washington, treat table at Hicksville), and your supply chain is running tight. Hicksville especially needs restocking\u2014five items out and seven at reorder level. Recommend immediate replenishment on large pink bags, Quick Dry, and the treat table before you miss sales on the momentum you've built."
